From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:58:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Cantilever Case 7: face-truss bars as deep as the TO's
 members

The trusses' depth is the TO's (H - b) and the member widths are scaled by one
factor to keep the volume; wide shallow bars had left an 18 mm gap between the
faces (2490 mm^3 of TO material missed). Detail 4: -3.5 %, overlap 79/79 %.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BdLZZ8R4FqXDzDRWDvVnZQ
